    "deduction": "Where the tangent span of g_2 + scaling at the basepoint z_0 has the dimension of the boundary orbit and spans C^15 together with the slice, the map (xi, s) -> exp(xi) s from a complement of the stabilizer algebra times the slice is a local biholomorphism at (0, z_0) by the inverse function theorem. Every z near z_0 is g(z) s(z) with g(z) -> identity and s(z) in the slice; the source stratum is invariant under G_2(C) x C^*, so s(z) lies in the source slice germ, and ker C_z = g(z) ker C_(s(z)). The limits of ker C_z along any sequence or continuous path in the source tending to z_0 are therefore limits along the slice germ (the fiber over z_0 of the closed graph equals that of its restriction to the slice; s(z(t)) is analytic and need not be semialgebraic), and the fiber over g z_0 is g applied to the fiber over z_0. G_2(C) x C^* is a direct factor of the connected group G_2(C) x SO(2, C) x C^* whose orbit is the boundary orbit, so its tangent rank is constant along that orbit; its orbits inside the boundary orbit are then open and partition a connected set, so the orbit of z_0 under G_2(C) x C^* is the whole boundary orbit.",
